111:The Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule 8,18 (ADOS) was administered to measure the impact of current, clinically observed core symptoms of autism. Where ADOS-G 8 or ADOS2 18 scores from previous assessments were available (within the past 12 months for children and  past  18 months  for  all  other  schedules),  these  assessments  were  not  repeated,  and  we accepted the historical ADOS-G (N=15) and historical ADOS-2 (N=3) scores from medical records.  To  allow  comparability  with  ADOS-2,  ADOS-G  raw  scores  were  mapped  onto ADOS-2 raw scores and calibrated severity scores (CSS) were computed 19 . In addition, whilst
113:most ADOS administrations were using ADOS-2 and not ADOS-G (due to the WPS published manual being available at different points in time following the US publication in 2012) a small number of participants had ADOS-G (N=1) and not ADOS-2 scores used. Based on ADOS-2 algorithm totals 20,21 , we report ADOS-2 Calibrated Severity Score (CSS) for 'Social Affect' indexing  social-communication  difficulties  and  'RRBs'  indexing  restricted  and  repetitive behaviours. The CSS scores range from 1 to 10, with higher scores indicating more severe ASD symptom severity.
