44220_2024_349_MOESM1_ESM.pdf.md:370:Supplementary Fig. 5 . We ran two separate canonical correlation analyses (CCA) to model the  relationship  between  multimodal  independent  components  (ICs)  and  either  a)  socialcommunicative  features  related  to  autism  or  b)  non-social  features  related  to  autism  (e.g., restricted  repetitive  behaviours).  We  tested  robustness  of  the  CCA  across  slightly  varying degrees of multimodality by changing the multimodality threshold ranging between 85%-99% (by steps of 1%). Results for both associations remained stable.
44220_2024_349_MOESM1_ESM.pdf.md:376:Supplementary Fig. 6 . Spatial and temporal characterization of IC37 . Spatial and temporal patterns of the different neuroimaging modalities associated with IC37. 6a shows the spatial and  temporal  Z-maps  thresholded  at  the  95th  percentile.  6b-e  depict  the  spatial  overlap  of suprathreshold voxels with a probabilistic functional atlas of the occipito-temporal cortex (i.e., VIS-atlas). 6f-i show the spatial overlap of suprathreshold voxels with the structural HarvardOxford  atlas  (HOA)  and  the  four  fusiform  gyrus  subregions  (i.e.,  anterior  and  posterior divisions of the temporal FC, temporal occipital FC and occipital FG). Here, 6b/f and 6c/g show the positive loadings and 6d/h and 6e/i the negative loadings, whereas 6b/f and 6d/h depict the left hemisphere  and 6c/g and 6e/i the right hemisphere. Abbreviations : IC=independent  component;  VIS=  probabilistic  functional  atlas  of  the  occipito-temporal cortex;  HOA=Harvard-Oxford  atlas;  FC=fusiform  cortex;  FG=fusiform  gyrus;  R=right; L=left; NAI=non-autistic individuals.
