44220_2024_349_MOESM1_ESM.pdf.md:390:Supplementary Fig. 8 . Spatial and temporal characterization of IC34. Spatial and temporal patterns of the different neuroimaging modalities associated with IC38. 8a shows the spatial and  temporal  Z-maps  thresholded  at  the  95th  percentile.  8b-e  depict  the  spatial  overlap  of suprathreshold voxels with a probabilistic functional atlas of the occipito-temporal cortex (i.e., VIS-atlas). 8f-i show the spatial overlap of suprathreshold voxels with the structural HarvardOxford  atlas  (HOA)  and  the  four  fusiform  gyrus  subregions  (i.e.,  anterior  and  posterior divisions of the temporal FC, temporal occipital FC and occipital FG). Here, 8b/f and 8c/g show the positive loadings and 8d/h and 8e/i the negative loadings, whereas Fig. 8b/f and 8d/h depict  the  left  hemisphere  and  Fig.  8c/g  and  8e/i  the  right  hemisphere. Abbreviations : IC=independent  component;  VIS=  probabilistic  functional  atlas  of  the  occipito-temporal cortex;  HOA=Harvard-Oxford  atlas;  FC=fusiform  cortex;  FG=fusiform  gyrus;  R=right; L=left; NAI=non-autistic individuals.
